Interpretation: pre-state size = old size = \old(this.size()). If index satisfies 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()), then for all i with 0 <= i && i < index, the element after operation at position i (this.elementAt(i) or get(i)?) remains unchanged, i.e., equals old element. But also "or is null if it was originally null." That's just equality (null stays null), so we can assert equality.

